WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.624
Hi! I'm Frank. Today I'm volunteering with my mom in San Francisco.

2
00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:14.509
San Francisco is a wealthy city, but it has many homeless people.

3
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.686
Thousands of homeless people live on the streets.

4
00:00:17.687 --> 00:00:20.758
They have limited access to bathrooms.

5
00:00:20.759 --> 00:00:25.939
Imagine that you couldn't take showers or use clean bathrooms.

6
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.990
I'm sure you wouldn't like that.

7
00:00:27.991 --> 00:00:32.147
But it's a common situation for homeless people.

8
00:00:32.148 --> 00:00:34.813
Doniece Sandoval is changing that.

9
00:00:34.814 --> 00:00:38.551
One day she heard a homeless woman crying.

10
00:00:38.552 --> 00:00:41.004
"I'm so filthy."

11
00:00:41.005 --> 00:00:43.648
The homeless woman sobbed.

12
00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:49.283
"I have nowhere to take a shower."

13
00:00:49.284 --> 00:00:52.863
This gave Doniece the idea for a shower bus.

14
00:00:52.864 --> 00:00:54.473
What's a shower bus?

15
00:00:54.474 --> 00:01:01.655
Follow me! I'll give you a tour.

16
00:01:01.656 --> 00:01:04.466
Mr. Jones is the bus driver.

17
00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:09.545
He drives the bus to different places around the city.

18
00:01:09.546 --> 00:01:12.973
The shower bus used to be a normal city bus.

19
00:01:12.974 --> 00:01:17.103
But now it has two private bathrooms.

20
00:01:17.104 --> 00:01:20.889
Each bathroom has its own shower, sink, and toilet.

21
00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:26.641
The bus also provides towels, soap, toothbrushes, and toothpaste.

22
00:01:26.642 --> 00:01:30.743
And they're all free!

23
00:01:30.744 --> 00:01:36.473
The shower bus changes lives.

24
00:01:36.474 --> 00:01:42.629
Being clean is very important, and not just for health reasons.

25
00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:46.513
Many homeless people can't get jobs if they aren't clean.

26
00:01:46.514 --> 00:01:50.891
Without jobs, they can't find housing.

27
00:01:50.892 --> 00:01:55.457
Being clean provides opportunities for many homeless people.

28
00:01:55.458 --> 00:01:59.170
In fact, the shower bus even changed my life.

29
00:01:59.171 --> 00:02:02.132
My mom and I used to be homeless.

30
00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:05.869
We couldn't take showers or use clean bathrooms.

31
00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:09.074
That was before we found the shower bus.

32
00:02:09.075 --> 00:02:19.261
On the shower bus, we could do both!

33
00:02:19.262 --> 00:02:24.822
It helped my mom find a job.

34
00:02:24.823 --> 00:02:27.517
It also helped us find an apartment.

35
00:02:27.518 --> 00:02:31.363
Then we weren't homeless anymore!

36
00:02:31.364 --> 00:02:35.102
But we still come to the shower bus to volunteer.

37
00:02:35.103 --> 00:02:37.696
That's it for our tour.

38
00:02:37.697 --> 00:02:44.365
Mr. Jones has to drive the bus to another part of the city.

39
00:02:44.366 --> 00:02:47.331
I'm glad you visited the shower bus with me.

40
00:02:47.332 --> 00:02:54.354
Maybe you can find a way to help the homeless too!

